<newsitem itemid="559183" id="root" date="1997-05-05" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Altech year earnings, dividend rise.</title>
<headline>Altech year earnings, dividend rise.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Feb 28, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   700	   vs 635</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     750	   vs 51</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 380	   vs 330</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   76.40	 vs 5.13</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain	5.12	  vs 76.93 charge</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   171.01	vs 49.19</p>
<p>    Tax			 61.53	 vs 40.46</p>
<p>    Interest received     32.85	 vs 15.86</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,921.43    vs 1,592.91</p>
<p>Div payable June 2</p>
<p>on register May 23</p>
<p>Full name: Allied Technologies Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The previous heavy exceptional charge reflected the write-off of industrialisation expenditure. The latest iear's gains followed a surplus on the disposal of investments.</p>
<p>Altech said order books were at a high level and the current year was likely to see real growth. The company said it had large cash resources and unissued equity and would be more pro-active on acquisitions</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
